course: dictionary
lesson: 14348
title: Officiate: who is in charge?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you who is in charge. «The vicar officiated at my cousin's wedding.» The sentence does not say the vicar got married or sang a song. It says the vicar was in charge of the wedding ceremony.
explain: Officiate means to lead an event as the person in charge. At church, a priest, minister or vicar officiates at weddings and funerals. In sport, a referee, umpire or judge officiates the game. Ask yourself: who makes the important decisions here?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The referee officiated the football match.» If you put "was in charge of" in place of officiated, the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Officiate is a verb. You can say I officiate, he officiates, they officiated, or officiating.
fact: «Officiate» means to be in charge of a ceremony or a game.
fact: At church, a vicar, priest or minister can officiate at a wedding, funeral or service.
fact: In sport, a referee, umpire or judge officiates a match.
fact: When you meet officiate, look for the clue: who is leading the event?
exercise: «The vicar officiated at my cousin's wedding.» Who officiated? | My cousin | The cake | The guests | *The vicar
exercise: «The umpire officiated the cricket match.» What did the umpire do? | Batted first for the team | Sold drinks to the crowd | *Was in charge of the game and made the decisions | Watched the match from home
exercise: Ava says officiate means to play in the game. Is she right? | Yes, officiate means to play in a team | *No, to officiate is to be in charge, not to play | No, officiate means to sleep during the match | Yes, officiate means to cheer for the players
test: «The referee officiated the football match.» Who is in charge of the game? | *The referee | The goalkeeper | The crowd | The players
test: At a funeral, what does it mean to officiate? | To sit at the back | To sing the loudest | To dig the grave | *To lead the service
exam: Which person might officiate a sports match? | A gardener | A chef | A hairdresser | *A referee
